==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat Guild Heroes''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cat Quest Heroes''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Heavenly Cat Heroes''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], Behemoth Stones, and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Cat Clan Heroes are cheap to produce and spammable for Uber standards, as well as being able to deal fair damage with rebound attacks, making them a decent all-round Uber. Their [[Critical Hit]] chance is very low (3%) and not to be relied upon. However, if you get lucky, it can deal a decent amount of damage to all enemies, especially [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]].

In terms of Cat Clan Heroes' survivability pre-True Form, they are immensely lacking, as they only have three knockbacks, a low standing range of 350, and only 24k HP at level 30, which is very bad for their standing range. On another note, their [[Weaken|Weaken]] ability is prone to being taken advantage of by many enemies; primarily due to their low uptime, which only lasts for half of their attack rate, meaning their ability to crowd-control is barely useful, and is outclassed by [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] due to her spammability and [[Talents]].

==='''True Form'''===
Cat Quest Heroes gain Relic targeting, Curse immunity, a longer weaken duration and doubled HP. The Relic targeting expands their usage on to Relic enemies, and their Curse immunity ability further solidifies this, being critical to many higher-difficulty [[Legend Stages]] that back their target traits with Relics. Doubled health greatly increases their survivability, and they really need it to handle the extreme DPS of the enemies faced by this point.

The Weaken is only improved by one second, but it's an improvement nonetheless, considering their low recharge time can allow them to be stacked in certain stages. Overall, this True Form is worth getting, as [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]] debuffers are incredibly useful in [[Uncanny Legends]] and exceedingly rare to come upon. With this being said, this True Form is not a high priority use of your Elder Catfruit, as certain [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks Cats]] will improve significantly more. Luckily, they have an advantage wherein they only need an Elder Seed instead of the entire fruit, although they also require an Epic Seed as well.

For obvious reasons, the increase of one second for their Weaken duration only slightly fixes the initial problem, so the only real prompt to get their True Form is for their new targeting.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Right off the bat, the exorbitant Gold Catfruit Seed cost of this Ultra Form means it is ideal to consider [[:Category:Cats evolving using Gold Catfruit Seeds|all your options]] before gunning directly for Heavenly Cat Heroes.

That being said, Heavenly Cat Heroes is actually quite well-rounded, basically doubling their DPS through [[Explosion]]s while gaining multiple other stat increases across the board. They gain an average DPS of 12,000, accounting for Critical Hits at Lv.60, which, while still not the best, is more than viable enough to let them finally play an attacking role in your lineup. Their HP also sees a substantial 19% boost, in addition to a tiny buff in their Weaken uptime brought about via Explosion, both of which majorly improves their endurance overall. You can expect them to stay on the field for quite a long time against target traits.

Finally, they receive [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]]; a simple situational improvement to specific matchups against enemies like [[Berserkory]], [[Bun Bun Symbiote]], [[Two Can]], [[Haniwanwan]], among others in mixed stages. A worthwhile improvement! Though their cost can offset many of the positives.

==='''Talents'''===
Dodge grants Cat Quest Heroes improved survivability, though it is luck-based. Toxic Immunity also improves their survivability against [[:Category:Enemies with Toxic ability|enemies with Toxic attacks]], though when it comes to their target traits, this would only work against [[Gobble]], [[Zollow]] and [[Casaurian Darkjo]]. Even then, however, these enemies already have a large number of designated counters, amongst them cheap and disposable alternatives, meaning it costs too much for what it does.

Resist Weaken is a waste of NP. Cat Quest Heroes are typically used for weakening enemies, meaning weaken effects don't impact their utility as much. HP Buff and Attack Buff are mediocre improvements. Again, while it is usually good to have higher stats, [[Catseye]]s are often the way to go. Since they don't work well as attackers outside of their ultra form, it is recommended not to invest in these at all unless you have paid the expensive price for their full potential.

